 the generalized-identity approach untouched. Even if truthmaking is only a neighboring relation, the self-grounding and mutual-grounding cases show why a theory should earn its asymmetry and transitivity constraints rather than build them in from the idea of explanation alone.\\\",\n            \\\"parent_ref\\\": \\\"draft-004\\\",\n            \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n                \\\"score\\\": 24,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Responds directly to the prior objection and fairly draws a broader methodological lesson from the source.\\\"\n            }\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\nwith output_json_path.open('w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    json.dump(payload, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    f.write('\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
